                <pb facs="0700" n="618" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg618"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 704.9312/10.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                        Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-07-05"><hi rendition="#italic">July 5,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 408.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 667 of
                    June 19, 1911, reporting the effort made by you to secure protection for the
                    lives and property of Americans and Chinese at Tapachula, Mexico. Your action is
                    approved.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
